      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so basically i'm just moving the \"extra\" stuff that doesn't belong to the main key into its own home so the main table stays clean. are there any common pitfalls or \"messy\" things i should watch out for when i'm doing this split? like what usually trips people up during the migration?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, a common pitfall is failing to maintain foreign key constraints when moving attributes, which can lead to orphaned records if you don't add a corresponding key in the new \"home\" table. You should also be careful not to lose audit history; if the new table is created too late, you might inadvertently overwrite historical data about departments or managers that existed before the split. Finally, remember to handle any pagination or performance implications, as denormalized data sometimes helps queries that ECRLI otherwise might slow down.",
      "source": "target",
